  "prefLabel": "Plc 1806.07 Certified Property Assessor Supervisor Duties",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1806.07 Certified Property Assessor Supervisor Duties. A certified property assessor supervisor may:\n\n(a) Perform and supervise all assessing services;\n\n(b) Conduct and supervise a revaluation, cyclical revaluation, or partial update by:\n\n(1) Compiling the data collection manual;\n\n(2) Performing a market analysis for the establishment of the base values and tables for the computer-assisted mass appraisal models;\n\n(3) Calibrating the computer-assisted mass appraisal models;\n\n(4) Performing the data quality final field review of the mass appraisal results;\n\n(5) Conducting statistical testing;\n\n(6) Completing and certifying a USPAP-compliant report; and\n\n(7) Overseeing and supervising:\n\na. The informal review process;\n\nb. The abatement review; and\n\nc. Defense of the appraised value(s);\n\n(c) Oversee any revaluation by assisting the municipal assessing officials to ensure that:\n\n(1) The revaluation is performed in accordance with applicable state statutes and administrative rules; and\n\n(2) The terms and conditions of the assessing services contract are adhered to; and\n\n(d) Submit signed and dated statements to the OPLC attesting to the qualifications at all classifications of certification to be true, accurate, and correct.\n\nSource. #14330, eff 9-22-25, EXPIRES: 9-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1800.html"
}
